From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Scrumpper <190908034+Scrumpper@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 22:39:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 33/59] drm/bridge: dw-hdmi-qp: CEC sink EDID check with the
 6.1 block rules

The 6.12 port of the CEC hardening (series 0005) replaced
drm_edid_block_valid(), static on 6.12, with a local check: perfect
header on the base block and a zero checksum on every block. 6.1
accepts more: a base header with at least 6 of 8 bytes right (repaired
in place, drm edid_fixup default), a CTA extension whose checksum is
wrong (switches and extenders mangle it), and it rejects all-zero
blocks and base blocks with an EDID major version other than 1. A sink
with a bad CTA checksum got its CEC physical address on 6.1 and none on
6.12 t1-t5 (the cec_phys_addr parameter was the only way out).

Apply the 6.1 rules in dw_hdmi_qp_edid_block_ok(). Override EDIDs are
not read here, so the change affects only the sink's own EDID. 6.12 t6.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01P6itje71iKPFBX7YKkfvRo
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/synopsys/dw-hdmi-qp.c | 19 +++++++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/synopsys/dw-hdmi-qp.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/synopsys/dw-hdmi-qp.c
index d2f2c566a..1e7bdafff 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/synopsys/dw-hdmi-qp.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/synopsys/dw-hdmi-qp.c
@@ -411,17 +411,28 @@ struct dw_hdmi_qp {
 	struct dentry *debugfs_compat;	/* /sys/kernel/debug/dw-hdmi%d symlink */
 };
 
-/* drm_edid_block_valid() is static on 6.12: header (base block) and checksum */
-static bool dw_hdmi_qp_edid_block_ok(const u8 *block, int i)
+/* 6.1 drm_edid_block_valid() rules (static on 6.12): header fixup, CTA checksum tolerated */
+static bool dw_hdmi_qp_edid_block_ok(u8 *block, int i)
 {
+	static const u8 header[8] = { 0x00, 0xff, 0xff, 0xff, 0xff, 0xff, 0xff, 0x00 };
 	u8 sum = 0;
 	int n;
 
-	if (!i && drm_edid_header_is_valid(block) != 8)
+	if (!memchr_inv(block, 0, EDID_LENGTH))
 		return false;
+	if (!i) {
+		/* drm edid_fixup default: 6 of 8 header bytes */
+		if (drm_edid_header_is_valid(block) < 6)
+			return false;
+		memcpy(block, header, sizeof(header));
+	}
 	for (n = 0; n < EDID_LENGTH; n++)
 		sum += block[n];
-	return sum == 0;
+	if (sum)
+		/* CTA extension (tag 0x02): switches mangle its checksum */
+		return i && block[0] == 0x02;
+	/* base block: EDID major version 1 only */
+	return i || block[0x12] == 1;
 }
 
 /* CEC PA is assigned by the sink: read its own EDID, an override EDID carries another PA */
